    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Observe mode (semgrep.mode = observe)",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 37,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 1
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read the observe panels",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 38,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "In observe mode the engine runs in the background and **never changes a reply**: Gitleaks decides alone, and the engine adds no latency. These panels show what enforce mode would have changed. Watch them for 7 days before the switch to enforce.\n\n- **would_deny** is a finding of the engine on a request that Gitleaks allowed. Triage each rule id in the pod log (`semgrep tier observed a finding`) as a true positive or a false positive.\n- **would_fail** is an engine failure (timeout, error, shed, breaker open, oversize). In enforce mode with failure mode deny, each one is a 503.\n- Compare the engine p95 with the deadline. See the README of the egress scanner for the exit criteria. No data in these panels means that the tier is off or in enforce mode."
      }
    },
